{
  "info": {
    "name": "Retail Promotion Scraper",
    "description": "Scrape competitor pricing and promotions.\n\nA scrape takes 1-40 minutes, far longer than an HTTP request survives, so POST /scrape returns immediately with a job started and the work continues in the background. Poll `GET /runs/latest/{retailer_key}` until status is no longer \"running\".\n\nStart the server:\n\n    .venv/Scripts/uvicorn api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n\nSet the `baseUrl` variable if it is not on localhost.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "description": "Where the API is running."
    },
    {
      "key": "run_id",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Filled in automatically by 'Latest run' once a run has started."
    },
    {
      "key": "retailer_key",
      "value": "boots",
      "description": "Folder-name form of the retailer: boots, john_lewis, marks_and_spencer, allbeauty, asos, amazon_uk, lookfantastic, next."
    },
    {
      "key": "job_id",
      "value": "",
      "description": "A queued job's id, from GET /queue."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Discover",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Is the API up, how many runs are on disk, and which retailers are crawling right now."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List retailers",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/retailers",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "retailers"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The 8 adapters, what each supports, and whether it is currently running.\n\n`supports_categories` - can honour a --categories filter.\n`confirms_brand_stocking` - can tell 'not stocked' from 'we found nothing'.\n`has_campaign_hubs` - campaigns_only will work."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Start a scrape",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Scrape one brand (quick test)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('retailer_key', body.retailer_key);",
                  "console.log('Started. Poll: ' + body.poll);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"retailer\": \"allbeauty\",\n  \"brands\": [\"Clinique\"],\n  \"max_products\": 5\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/scrape",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape"
              ]
            },
            "description": "AllBeauty is the fastest retailer (under a minute), so it is the one to test with.\n\n`max_products` caps products PER BRAND. Omit it for a full run.\n\nReturns 202 with a `poll` URL. It does NOT wait for the crawl."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Scrape all seven brands (full run)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"retailer\": \"boots\",\n  \"brands\": [\n    \"Clinique\",\n    \"MAC\",\n    \"Tom Ford\",\n    \"Jo Malone\",\n    \"Estee Lauder\",\n    \"Bobbi Brown\",\n    \"Too Faced\"\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/scrape",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A real run. Boots takes roughly 35 minutes.\n\nBrand spellings are corrected automatically: \"Bobbie Brown\" becomes \"Bobbi Brown\"."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Campaigns only (no products)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"retailer\": \"marksandspencer\",\n  \"campaigns_only\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/scrape",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Every promotion the retailer is running, regardless of brand. No brands needed.\n\nFast - it only reads the offers pages. M&S returns about 29 campaigns."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Scrape with options",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"retailer\": \"https://www.lookfantastic.com\",\n  \"brands\": [\"Clinique\", \"MAC\"],\n  \"categories\": [\"skincare\"],\n  \"strict_brand\": true,\n  \"max_products\": 20,\n  \"refusal_limit\": 0.45\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/scrape",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Every command-line flag is available.\n\n`retailer` accepts a name, a domain or a full URL.\n`categories` - only for retailers where supports_categories is true.\n`strict_brand` - only accept brands proved by structured data. Fewer records, higher confidence.\n`refusal_limit` - share of refused requests before the run is called failed (default 0.30)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Duplicate request -> 409",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"retailer\": \"allbeauty\",\n  \"brands\": [\"Clinique\"]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/scrape",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Send this WHILE the same retailer is running OR queued.\n\nReturns 409 with the existing job, rather than queueing it twice -- asking again is a duplicate request, not a second crawl."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Watch it run",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Latest run for a retailer",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.run_id) { pm.collectionVariables.set('run_id', body.run_id); }",
                  "console.log('status: ' + body.status + '  products: ' + (body.products ?? '-'));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs/latest/{{retailer_key}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "runs",
                "latest",
                "{{retailer_key}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Poll this after starting a scrape. Saves the run_id into a collection variable, so the requests below just work.\n\n`running: true`   still crawling\n`status: ok`      finished, data is good\n`status: failed`  finished, but do not trust it - see `reason`\n`status: incomplete`  the run was killed part-way"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "All runs",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs?limit=20",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "runs"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20"
                },
                {
                  "key": "retailer",
                  "value": "boots",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Every run, newest first. Add `retailer` to filter."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Run details (manifest)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs/{{run_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "runs",
                "{{run_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The full record of one run: status, reason, product and campaign counts, requests made and refused, duration, brands that returned nothing, and any warnings.\n\nThis is the row worth keeping in a warehouse."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Run log",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs/{{run_id}}/log?tail=200",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "runs",
                "{{run_id}}",
                "log"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "tail",
                  "value": "200"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Plain text, every request the crawl made. The first place to look when a run fails."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Read the data",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Products",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs/{{run_id}}/products",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "runs",
                "{{run_id}}",
                "products"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "brand",
                  "value": "Clinique",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Every product from the run. Enable `brand` to filter to one.\n\nEach record carries: current_price, original_price, discount_percent, currency, availability, promotional_copy, applied_campaigns, and brand_verified_by - which records HOW the brand was proved."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Campaigns",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs/{{run_id}}/campaigns",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "runs",
                "{{run_id}}",
                "campaigns"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Promotions the retailer is running.\n\n`scope` says how widely each applies:\n  sitewide   - a banner on every page\n  brand      - tied to one brand\n  category   - tied to a department\n  product    - tied to one item\n  unresolved - found it, cannot prove its reach"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Rejected records",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs/{{run_id}}/rejected",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "runs",
                "{{run_id}}",
                "rejected"
              ]
            },
            "description": "What the run refused to publish, and why: missing_price, brand_mismatch, discount_mismatch, unverified_brand.\n\nRejections are output on purpose - you can see what was refused rather than wondering why a count looks low."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Compare retailers",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Compare everything scraped",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"threshold\": 0.85\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/compare",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "compare"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Where one retailer undercuts another on the same product - the question the project exists to answer.\n\nUses the newest successful run of every retailer. Needs at least two.\n\n`threshold` is title similarity, 0-1. Lower it for more matches, at the cost of pairing products that only read alike.\n\nCheck two flags before quoting a gap:\n  rrp_disagreement  - the shops disagree on the RRP, so these may be different products\n  currency_mismatch - not all offers were in one currency"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Compare two named retailers",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"retailers\": [\"boots\", \"lookfantastic\"],\n  \"threshold\": 0.85\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/compare",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "compare"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Same thing, limited to the retailers you name. Use the folder-name form: boots, john_lewis, marks_and_spencer, allbeauty, asos, amazon_uk, lookfantastic."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. The queue",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Queue status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/queue",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "queue"
              ]
            },
            "description": "What is running, what is waiting, and what finished recently.\n\nRetailers run ONE AT A TIME on purpose. Several browser-driven crawls at once starve each other of DNS and network -- three together turned a 54-minute Lookfantastic run into 30 hours.\n\n  running  - the crawl in progress, or null\n  queued   - waiting, in the order they will run\n  recent   - the last 20 finished, newest first\n\nJob status mirrors run.py's exit codes: ok, failed, skipped, cancelled, stopped.",
            "header": []
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Queue three at once",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/scrape",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "scrape"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Send this three times, changing `retailer` each time. All three are accepted immediately; only the first starts.\n\nThe response tells you where you are:\n  position        place in the queue\n  will_start_now  true only for the first\n\nSo you can fire all seven retailers and forget about ordering.",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"retailer\": \"marksandspencer\",\n  \"brands\": [\n    \"Clinique\"\n  ],\n  \"max_products\": 5\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "console.log(b.retailer + ' -> position ' + b.position + ', starts now: ' + b.will_start_now);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Stop the running scrape",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/queue/stop",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "queue",
                "stop"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Stops the crawl in progress. Anything queued behind it still runs.\n\nThe retailer's lock is cleared as part of stopping -- without that it would sit on disk and the next six hours of runs for that retailer would be skipped as 'already running'.\n\nProducts already flushed to products.partial.jsonl survive, so a stopped crawl still leaves what it had collected. There is no manifest, which is itself the signal the run did not finish.\n\nReturns {\"stopped\": null} if nothing was running.",
            "header": []
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Stop everything",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/queue/stop?clear_queue=true",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "queue",
                "stop"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "clear_queue",
                  "value": "true"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Stops the current crawl AND drops everything still waiting.\n\nUse before a deploy or a restart.",
            "header": []
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Cancel a queued job",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/queue/{{job_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "queue",
                "{{job_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Removes one job that has NOT started yet.\n\nTake the job_id from GET /queue -> queued[].job_id.\n\nA job already running is left alone -- use POST /queue/stop for that. Returns 404 if the job has started or does not exist.",
            "header": []
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
